# The SPA's response headers for every path. The `shift-web` image (story
# 20.3, deploy/web/) serves this block, as built, on every response, errors
# included: its nginx header lines are rendered from the BUILT dist/_headers at
# image build, so only one `/*` block may exist, with no `!` detach. The build
# appends the Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only line, derived from
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL and the page's inline scripts
# (apps/web/src/lib/content-security-policy.ts). HSTS: one year, subdomains,
# no preload. Cloudflare Pages reads the same file while it is still used.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), usb=(), browsing-topics=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
